{"t": 1795072666.120944, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The PHP upgrade to 8.3 caused fatal errors with the **limit-login-attempts-reloaded** plugin, resulting in 500 errors on the homepage and sample post page. The WordPress admin area itself remains accessible.\n\nPer rule R6, I cannot deactivate incompatible plugins myself. The upgrade must stop here.\n\nTo proceed safely, you'll need to either:\n1. Update or replace **limit-login-attempts-reloaded** with a PHP 8.3-compatible version, **or**\n2. Temporarily disable the plugin via wp-cli or WP admin after backing up the site.\n\nOnce the plugin issue is resolved, you can retest PHP 8.3 compatibility. I have not changed any production settings—only dev was modified. Let me know how you'd like to proceed."}
{"t": 1795072666.121152, "kind": "stop", "reason": "end_turn"}
